OBSERVATION: --file bypasses the 'already complete, skipping' check that plain
'cappv1 start' applies during bulk discovery - it always re-processes/re-saves
the named file. Per-slide progress is still honored (no slides were recaptioned
here, all 4 were already done in state, so this was a fast re-save, zero API
cost) but the file gets rewritten to output/ every time --file names it. This
is a real, working distinction between the two invocation modes, not a bug.

