GAP OBSERVED: an invalid --file crashes before any logger.info() call fires.
setup_logging() already created (empty) logs/run-20260903-140005.log by the
time discover_files() raises, so bin/cappv1's auto-attach finds and tails
that real-but-forever-empty file - the live view shows 'Live progress...'
and then nothing, silently, forever. The actual FileNotFoundError traceback
only appears in logs/cappv1-launcher.log, which nothing points the user to
in this specific failure path. Related to, but distinct from, the corrupt-
state.json crash already tracked in TODO-security.md. Not fixed now - noting
for later per today's scope (test first, fix later).

